    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9179" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cŏlubrīnus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		coluber, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>like a serpent;</i> trop., <i>cunning</i>, <i>wily</i> (ante- and post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ingenio esse,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut.
					Truc. 4, 3, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vis gestūs,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Spect. 18</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cŏlubrīna</span></b> , ae,
				f., <i>a plant</i>, <i>also called</i> bryonia <i>and</i> dracontea,
					<i><span class="en">App. Herb. 14</span></i>.</div>
